Subject: local: allow the conformance emulator in the GitHub code profile

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. This is a Breadboard-local substitution, recorded under
decision 3 of the Fullsend integration conformance plan.

A provider profile is the sandbox's network allowlist. Fullsend imports
profiles verbatim and expands no variables in them, which is the right
behaviour for a policy file: an environment variable should not be able to
widen what a sandbox may reach. The consequence is that a host which varies
per environment cannot be templated, and the conformance forge is a GitHub
emulator on a cluster address.

So the emulator's host is added explicitly. The posture is unchanged:
read-only, enforced, and the binary allowlist still excludes curl so the agent
cannot make raw HTTP calls with the injected token.

This profile backs the code and fix agents. The read-only profile that backs
triage and review, fullsend-github-ro, is no longer in this repository: since
v0.52.0 fullsend embeds it in the binary under a reserved id, so a repository
copy cannot override it. Its half of this substitution therefore moved to the
fullsend build patch list as
deploy/fullsend/patches/0016-local-allow-the-emulator-in-the-embedded-github-ro-profile.patch.
Keep the two endpoint lists in sync.

If these profiles ever become templatable upstream, this patch should be
dropped rather than rebased.

Breadboard note: applied to the agents mirror by
deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py.

diff --git a/profiles/fullsend-github-code.yaml b/profiles/fullsend-github-code.yaml
index d683f04..153d52e 100644
--- a/profiles/fullsend-github-code.yaml
+++ b/profiles/fullsend-github-code.yaml
@@ -28,6 +28,33 @@ endpoints:
     protocol: rest
     access: read-only
     enforcement: enforce
+  # Breadboard-local: the conformance forge is a GitHub emulator on a cluster
+  # address, and this profile is the sandbox's network allowlist. Fullsend
+  # imports profiles verbatim and does not expand variables in them, which is
+  # correct for a policy file, so a host that varies per environment can only
+  # be added by editing it. That makes this a local substitution rather than
+  # something to send upstream.
+  #
+  # The read-only posture and the binary allowlist below are unchanged: curl
+  # stays excluded so the agent cannot make raw HTTP calls with the injected
+  # token, and these entries are enforced like the rest.
+  - host: github.local
+    port: 443
+    protocol: rest
+    access: read-only
+    enforcement: enforce
+  # github.com serves GraphQL from api.github.com/graphql. An enterprise host
+  # has no second hostname and serves it from the appliance at /api/graphql,
+  # which is the path gh posts to for any host that is not github.com. Copying
+  # the public entry's "/graphql" here allowed a path nothing asks for and
+  # denied the one that is used, so every GraphQL call the agent made was
+  # refused with policy_denied while the profile looked like it permitted them.
+  - host: github.local
+    port: 443
+    protocol: graphql
+    access: read-only
+    enforcement: enforce
+    path: "/api/graphql"
 binaries:
   - "**/gh"
   - "**/git"
